<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0016042> rdfs:label "late-onset isolated ACTH deficiency"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "Late-onset isolated ACTH deficiency is a rare, acquired, pituitary hormone deficiency characterized by secondary adrenal insufficiency, with normal secretion of anterior pituitary hormones, except for ACTH. Patients present with weakness, fatigue, weight loss, anorexia, vomiting/nausea, hypoglycemia, and abnormally low serum ACTH and cortisol levels. Association with autoimmune disease such as Hashimoto's thyroiditis has been described."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
