<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0017076> rdfs:label "posterior meningocele"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "Posterior meningocele is a rare neural tube closure defect characterized by the herniation of a cerebrospinal fluid-filled sac, that is lined by dura and arachnoid mater, through a posterior spina bifida and covered by a layer of skin of variable thickness, which may be dysplastic or ulcerated. The spinal cord and nerves are generally not included and function normally, although sometimes a tethered cord may be associated. They are most commonly located in the lumbar or sacral region."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:has_phenotype <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000238>,
