<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0017572> rdfs:label "tick-borne encephalitis" ;
    dcterms:description "Tick-borne encephalitis is caused by an arbovirus of the Flaviviridae family (tick-borne encephalitis virus, TBEV), transmitted principally by the bite of the Ixodes ricinus tick. The symptomology is biphasic, with the initial phase being associated with a flu-like illness and the second phase (occurring in less than 10% of patients) with symptoms of meningitis or, more rarely, meningoencephalitis." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Tick-borne viral encephalitis"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
