<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018959> rdfs:label "potassium-aggravated myotonia" ;
    dcterms:description "Potassium-aggravated myotonia (PAM) is a muscular channelopathy presenting with a pure myotonia dramatically aggravated by potassium ingestion, with variable cold sensitivity and no episodic weakness. This group includes three forms: myotonia fluctuans, myotonia permanens, and acetazolamide-responsive myotonia."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
