<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0021081> rdfs:label "anti-NMDA receptor encephalitis" ;
    dcterms:description "An autoimmune acute encephalitis caused by antibodies against the glutamate NMDA receptor. It usually affects females and in the majority of cases it is associated with the presence of a tumor, most commonly an ovarian teratoma. The presence of a tumor in patients with this form of encephalitis implies that the latter is a paraneoplastic syndrome. It is manifested with psychiatric symptoms and epileptic seizures. It is a potentially lethal disorder; however, it is usually reversible with the prompt removal of the tumor."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "anti-NMDA receptor encephalitis"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "limbic encephalitis with N-methyl-D-aspartate receptor antibodies"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "limbic encephalitis with NMDA receptor antibodies" ;
