    dcterms:description "A subtype of retinitis pigmentosa in which, instead of the pathology starting in the mid-periphery like typical retinitis pigmentosa, the disease starts in the near periphery closer to the vascular arcades and tends to spare the far periphery." ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
    ns1:xref "UMLS:C1849398"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> .

<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0007975> rdfs:label "Hypometric horizontal saccades" ;
    dcterms:description "Saccadic undershoot of horizontal saccadic eye movements, i.e., a horizontal saccadic eye movement that has less than the magnitude that would be required to gain fixation of the object."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
