<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0012796> rdfs:label "Increased cup-to-disc ratio"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "An elevation in the ratio of the diameter of the cup of the optic disc to the total diameter of the disk. The optic disc has an orange-pink rim with a pale center (the cup) that does not contain neuroretinal tissue. An increase in this ratio therefore may indicate a decrease in the quantity of healthy neuroretinal cells." ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Increased cup disc ratio"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
