<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005033> rdfs:label "ganglioneuroma" ;
    dcterms:description "A benign neuroblastic tumor of the sympathetic nervous system that occurs in childhood. Ganglioneuroma typically arises from the sympathetic trunk in the mediastinum. Histologic features include spindle cell proliferation (resembling a neurofibroma) and the presence of large ganglion cells. Common presenting features include a palpable abdominal mass, hepatomegaly, and a thoracic mass detected on routine chest X-ray." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "ganglioneuroma (Schwannian Stroma-dominant)"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
