<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005576> rdfs:label "cryoglobulinemia" ;
    dcterms:description "Cryoglobulinemia is a type of vasculitis that is caused by abnormal proteins (antibodies) in the blood called 'cryoglobulins.' At cold temperatures, these proteins become solid or gel-like, which can block blood vessels and cause a variety of health problems. Many people affected by this condition will not experience any unusual signs or symptoms. When present, symptoms vary but may include breathing problems; fatigue; glomerulonephritis ; joint or muscle pain; purpura ; Raynaud's phenomenon ; skin death; and/or skin ulcers. In some cases, the exact underlying cause is unknown; however, cryoglobulinemia can be associated with a variety of conditions including certain types of infection; chronic inflammatory diseases (such as autoimmune disease); and/or cancers of the blood or immune system. Treatment varies based on the severity of the condition, the symptoms present in each person and the underlying cause." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "cryoglobulinemia" ;
    ns1:synonym "cryoglobulinemia" ;
    ns1:xref "ICD10CM:D89.1"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "ICD9:273.2"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "MEDGEN:3673"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "MESH:D003449"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "DOID:2917",
        "EFO:0005846",
        "NCIT:C26736",
        "SCTID:30911005",
        "UMLS:C0010403" .

