<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008662> rdfs:label "autosomal dominant vitreoretinochoroidopathy"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "Autosomal dominant vitreoretinochoroidopathy (ADVIRC) is a genetic vitreous-retinal disease characterized by ocular developmental anomalies such as microcornea, a shallow anterior chamber, glaucoma and cataract. Abnormal chorioretinal pigmentation is present, usually lying between the vortex veins and the ora serrata for 360 degrees." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
