<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009717> rdfs:label "Schwartz-Jampel syndrome" ;
    dcterms:description "A rare, genetic neuromuscular disease characterized by permanent myotonia, mask-like facies (with blepharospasm, narrow palpebral fissures, small mouth with pursed lips and puckered chin) , and chondrodysplasia (variably manifesting with short stature, pectus carinatum, kyphoscoliosis, bowing of long bones, epiphyseal, metaphyseal, and hip dysplasia)." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Catel-Hempel type dysostosis enchondralis metaepiphysaria"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
