<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0010631> rdfs:label "incontinentia pigmenti"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "Incontinentia pigmenti (IP) is a rare X-linked dominant multi-systemic ectodermal dysplasia usually lethal in males and presenting neonatally in females with a bullous rash along Blashko's lines (BL) followed by verrucous plaques evolving over time to hyperpigmented swirling patterns. It is further characterized by teeth abnormalities, alopecia, nail dystrophy and affects occasionally the retina and the central nervous system (CNS)." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Bloch-Siemens syndrome"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "Incontinentia pigmenti syndrome"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "incontinentia pigmenti, X-linked dominant"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "Bloch-Sulzberger syndrome",
        "incontinentia pigmenti" ;
