<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0010878> rdfs:label "hereditary spastic paraplegia 6" ;
    dcterms:description "Autosomal dominant spastic paraplegia type 6 (SPG6) is a form of hereditary spastic paraplegia which usually presents in late adolescence or early adulthood as a pure phenotype of lower limb spasticity with hyperreflexia and extensor plantar responses, as well as mild bladder disturbances and pes cavus. Rarely, it can present as a complex phenotype with additional manifestations including epilepsy, variable peripheral neuropathy and/or memory impairment."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "SPG6"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "FSP3",
        "NIPA1 hereditary spastic paraplegia",
