<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011113> rdfs:label "Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 4C" ;
    dcterms:description "Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 4C (CMT4C) is a subtype of Charcot-Marie-Tooth type 4 characterized by childhood or adolescent-onset of a relatively mild, demyelinating sensorimotor neuropathy that contrasts with a severe, rapidly progressing, early-onset scoliosis, and the typical CMT phenotype (i.e. distal muscle weakness and atrophy, sensory loss, and often foot deformity). A wide spectrum of nerve conduction velocities are observed and cranial nerve involvement and kyphoscoliosis have also been reported." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 4 caused by mutation in SH3TC2"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
