<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011738> rdfs:label "bilateral frontoparietal polymicrogyria"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "A descriptive term reflecting increased gyral folding in the frontoparietal regions as determined by magnetic resonance imaging. It has subsequently been shown to represent a cobblestone malformation on histopathology. BFPP typically presents with hypotonia, developmental delay, moderate to severe intellectual disability, pyramidal signs, epileptic seizures, non-progressive cerebellar ataxia, deconjugate gaze, and/or strabismus."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
