<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011889> rdfs:label "Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2I" ;
    dcterms:description "Autosomal dominant Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2I (CMT2I) is a form of axonal Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, a peripheral sensorimotor neuropathy, characterized by a late onset with severe sensory loss (paresthesia and hypoesthesia) associated with distal weakness, mainly of the legs, and absent or reduced deep tendon reflexes." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, type 2I"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
