<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0012276> rdfs:label "generalized epilepsy-paroxysmal dyskinesia syndrome" ;
    dcterms:description "Generalized epilepsy-paroxysmal dyskinesia syndrome is characterized by the association of paroxysmal dyskinesia and generalized epilepsy (usually absence or generalized tonic-clonic seizures) in the same individual or family. The prevalence is unknown. Analysis in one of the reported families led to the identification of a causative mutation in the KCNMA1 gene (chromosome 10q22), encoding the alpha subunit of the BK channel. Transmission is autosomal dominant." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "GEPD" ;
    ns1:has_phenotype <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000565>,
