    dcterms:description "Spinocerebellar ataxia type 28 (SCA28) is a very rare subtype of type I autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxia (ADCA type I). It is characterized by juvenile onset, slowly progressive cerebellar ataxia due to Purkinje cell degeneration." ;
