<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0012639> rdfs:label "hereditary spastic paraplegia 18" ;
    dcterms:description "A rare, complex type of hereditary spastic paraplegia characterized by progressive spastic paraplegia (presenting in early childhood) associated with delayed motor development, severe intellectual disability and joint contractures. A thin corpus callosum is equally noted on brain magnetic resonance imaging. SPG18 is caused by a mutation in the ERLIN2 gene (8p11.2) encoding the protein, Erlin-2."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
