<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013212> rdfs:label "Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease axonal type 2N"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "Autosomal dominant Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2N (CMT2N) is a mild form of axonal Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, a peripheral sensorimotor neuropathy, characterized by distal legs sensory loss and weakness that can be asymmetric. Tendon reflexes are reduced in the knees and absent in ankles. Progression is slow." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
