<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013382> rdfs:label "progressive demyelinating neuropathy with bilateral striatal necrosis"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "Progressive polyneuropathy with bilateral striatal necrosis is a rare, genetic disorder of thiamine metabolism and transport characterized by the childhood-onset of recurrent episodes of flaccid paralysis and encephalopathy, associated with bilateral striatal necrosis and chronic progressive axonal polyneuropathy with proximal and distal muscle weakness, areflexia, contractures and foot deformities."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "thiamine metabolism dysfunction syndrome 4 (progressive polyneuropathy type)"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
