<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0014558> rdfs:label "autosomal dominant intellectual disability-craniofacial anomalies-cardiac defects syndrome" ;
    dcterms:description "A rare genetic neurodevelopmental disorder characterized by global developmental delay (DD) and variable degrees of intellectual disability (ID) with delayed or limited/absent speech development associated with neonatal hypotonia, feeding difficulties, cardiac anomalies and dysmorphic facial features, predominantly broad nasal tip and thin, tented upper lip. Microcephaly, frequent infections, gastrointestinal and/or ocular anomalies have also been described." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "autosomal dominant intellectual disability 32"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "Arboleda-Tham syndrome",
        "KAT6A Syndrome",
