<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0015349> rdfs:label "progressive cavitating leukoencephalopathy" ;
    dcterms:description "Progressive cavitating leukoencephalopathy is characterized by acute episodes of neurological deficit (ataxia, dysarthria, seizures) with irritability and opisthotonus followed by either steady deterioration or alternating periods of rapid progression and prolonged periods of stability." ;
