    dcterms:description "Attenuated Chédiak-Higashi syndrome (CHS) is a very rare and atypical form of CHS, a genetic disorder characterized by partial oculocutaneous albinism (OCA), severe immunodeficiency, mild bleeding, neurological dysfunction and lymphoproliferative disorder."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
