<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0800028> rdfs:label "dyskinesia with orofacial involvement, autosomal dominant" ;
    dcterms:description "A rare paroxysmal movement disorder, with childhood or adolescent onset, characterized by paroxysmal choreiform, dystonic, and myoclonic movements involving the limbs (mostly distal upper limbs), neck and/or face, which can progressively increase in both frequency and severity until they become nearly constant. Patients may also present with delayed motor milestones, perioral and periorbital dyskinesias, dysarthria, hypotonia, and weakness."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "dyskinesia, familial, with facial myokymia"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
