<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0003463> rdfs:label "Increased extraneuronal autofluorescent lipopigment"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "Lipofuscin, a generic term applied to autofluorescent lipopigment, is a mixture of protein and lipid that accumulates in most aging cells, particularly those involved in high lipid turnover (e.g., the adrenal medulla) or phagocytosis of other cell types (e g., the retinal pigment epithelium or RPE; macrophage). This term pertains if there is an increase in the extraneuronal accumulation of lipofuscin (also known as autofluorescent lipoprotein) more than expected for the age of the patient."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
    ns1:related_synonym "Lipopigment in extraneuronal cells" ;
