    dcterms:description "A complete duplication affecting one or more of the phalanges of the thumb. As opposed to a partial duplication were there is still a variable degree of fusion between the duplicated bones, a complete duplication leads to two separate bones appearing side to side (radio-ulnar axis) as seen on x-rays. A duplication leading to an accessory bone appearing in the proximo-distal axis on x-rays, this is actually a different entity called a Pseudoepiphyses (see according terms) sometimes also referred to as Hyperphalangism." ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Complete duplication of thumb bones"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
