<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0017579> rdfs:label "Baraitser-Winter cerebrofrontofacial syndrome" ;
    dcterms:description "Baraitser-Winter syndrome (BWS) is a malformation syndrome, characterized by facial dysmorphism (hypertelorism with ptosis, broad bulbous nose, ridged metopic suture, arched eyebrows, progressive coarsening of the face), ocular coloboma, pachygyria and/or band heterotopias with antero-posterior gradient, progressive joint stiffening, and intellectual deficit of variable severity, often with severe epilepsy. Pachygyria - epilepsy - intellectual disability - dysmorphism (Fryns-Aftimos syndrome (FA)) corresponds to the appearance of BWS in elderly patients." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Baraitser-Winter syndrome" ;
