<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0001709> rdfs:label "Third degree atrioventricular block" ;
    dcterms:description "Third-degree atrioventricular (AV) block (also referred to as complete heart block) is the complete dissociation of the atria and the ventricles. Third-degree AV block exists when more P waves than QRS complexes exist and no relationship (no conduction) exists between them." ;
