<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0007473> rdfs:label "Duane retraction syndrome"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "Duane retraction syndrome (DRS) is a congenital form of strabismus characterized by horizontal eye movement limitation, globe retraction and palpebral fissure narrowing in attempted adduction. It is caused by a failure of development of the abducens nerve and can lead to amblyopia." ;
