<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0008151> rdfs:label "Prolonged prothrombin time" ;
    dcterms:description "Increased time to coagulation in the prothrombin time test, which is a measure of the extrinsic pathway of coagulation. The results of the prothrombin time test are often expressed in terms of the International normalized ratio (INR), which is calculated as a ratio of the patient's prothrombin time (PT) to a control PT standardized for the potency of the thromboplastin reagent developed by the World Health Organization (WHO) using the formula: INR is equal to Patient PT divided by Control PT." ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Increased INR"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
        "Increased international normalized ratio"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype>,
