<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013099> rdfs:label "combined pituitary hormone deficiencies, genetic form"^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    dcterms:description "Congenital hypopituitarism is characterized by multiple pituitary hormone deficiency, including somatotroph, thyrotroph, lactotroph, corticotroph or gonadotroph deficiencies, due to mutations of pituitary transcription factors involved in pituitary ontogenesis. Congenital hypopituitarism is rare compared with the high incidence of hypopituitarism induced by pituitary adenomas, transsphenoidal surgery or radiotherapy." ;
    ns1:category ns1:Disease ;
