<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0006937> rdfs:label "Impaired distal tactile sensation" ;
    dcterms:description "A reduced sense of touch (tactile sensation) on the skin of the distal limbs. This is usually tested with a wisp of cotton or a fine camel's hair brush, by asking patients to say 'now' each time they feel the stimulus."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Decreased distal touch sense",
