<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000505> rdfs:label "Visual impairment" ;
    dcterms:description "Visual impairment (or vision impairment) is vision loss (of a person) to such a degree as to qualify as an additional support need through a significant limitation of visual capability resulting from either disease, trauma, or congenital or degenerative conditions that cannot be corrected by conventional means, such as refractive correction, medication, or surgery." ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
